#. module: servicereferralagreement
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:servicereferralagreement.sa_gfs_usa
msgid ""
"Estimated Travel Expenses: - Travel expenses are estimated and are \n"
"                subject to change based on actual travel expenses incurred.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                Travel expenses are on a direct reimbursement basis and include all expenses for transportation, \n"
"                accommodation and meals. Whenever possible trips are combined with other business and expenses \n"
"                are divided to reduce the total cost for all of our customers.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>1. DELIVERY.</b> Note that audit reports and certificates are sent electronically via email. \n"
"                Hardcopies are available.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>2. DATA OWNERSHIP.</b> All data submitted by Primus Auditing Ops into the PrimusGFS certification \n"
"                system operated by the scheme owner, becomes the property of Azzule Systems for use in preparing \n"
"                specific statistical comparisons, and generic use in reports, presentations and other materials.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>3. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY.</b> Customer hereby releases Primus Auditing Ops and Primus Group Inc. \n"
"                and their respective affiliates, from any loss or liability suffered by Customer, as defined below, \n"
"                resulting from services performed under this Agreement. Such release shall include any actual, incidental, \n"
"                consequential or other damages beyond amounts paid to Primus Auditing Ops for auditing performed and/or facilitated \n"
"                by Primus Auditing Ops. Customer further acknowledges and agrees that Primus Auditing Ops' liability is limited \n"
"                only to audit work performed by it, and the parties expressly acknowledge that Primus Auditing Ops is not liable \n"
"                for Customer's commodity, its safety, or quality.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>4. GOVERNING LAW / VENUE.</b> This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws \n"
"                of the State of California. In the event that it is necessary to institute any action to enforce any right granted \n"
"                herein or to redress any alleged breach hereof, then the exclusive venue for such action shall reside with the \n"
"                applicable Superior or Municipal Court located in Santa Maria, California.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>5. GLOBAL FOOD SAFETY INITIATIVE and PRIMUSGFS.</b>\n"
"                Customer expressly acknowledges that Primus Auditing Ops and its auditors are not a governing agency, and does \n"
"                not set the industry standards for safety or protocol. Customer also acknowledges that PrimusGFS is an audit \n"
"                program benchmarked and governed by the Global Food Safety Initiative's (GFSI) standards and promulgated requirements. \n"
"                All results posted by Primus Auditing Ops will be based on GFSI criteria. Customer expressly acknowledges that \n"
"                Primus Auditing Ops has not created these standards and criteria, but is only acting in accordance with GFSI."
msgstr ""

#. module: servicereferralagreement
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:servicereferralagreement.sa_smeta_usa
msgid ""
"Estimated Travel Expenses: - Travel expenses are estimated and are subject to change based on actual travel \n"
"                expenses incurred. Travel expenses are on a direct reimbursement basis and include all expenses for \n"
"                transportation, accommodation and meals. Whenever possible, trips are combined with other business and \n"
"                expenses are divided to reduce the total costs for all of our customers.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>1. DELIVERY.</b> Audit reports an information related to the audit are shared through the SEDEX Platform.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>2. TRANSFER OF DATA TO OUTSIDE PARTIES.</b> Primus Auditing Ops may be required to submit information obtained \n"
"                during the audit to either Supplier Ethical Data Exchange (\"SEDEX\") and/or to the Association of Professional Social \n"
"                Compliance Auditors (“APSCA”) for its authorized use. By executing this Agreement, Customer acknowledges that such \n"
"                information may be provided to the applicable SEDEX and/or APSCA, and consents to the transfer of such information.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>3. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY.</b> Customer hereby releases Primus Auditing Ops, its employees, directors, principals, \n"
"                agents, and affiliates, from any loss or liability suffered by Customer, resulting from services performed under this \n"
"                Agreement. Such release shall include any actual, incidental, consequential or other damages beyond amounts paid to Primus \n"
"                Auditing Ops for auditing performed and/or facilitated by Primus Auditing Ops. Customer further acknowledges and agrees \n"
"                that Primus Auditing Ops' liability is limited only to the audit work performed by it, and the parties expressly acknowledge \n"
"                that Primus Auditing Ops is not liable for Customer's commodity, its safety, or quality.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>4. GOVERNING LAW / VENUE.</b> This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State \n"
"                of California. In the event that it is necessary to institute any action to enforce any right granted herein or to redress \n"
"                any alleged breach hereof, then the exclusive venue for such action shall reside with the Superior Court located in Santa \n"
"                Maria, California.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>5. RIGHT TO REFERRAL.</b> Customer acknowledges that Primus Auditing Ops is, or may, contract out the auditing services \n"
"                performed for Customer. Because an independent auditor is engaged in his/her own independent contracting business and is \n"
"                not an employee of Primus Auditing Ops, if Primus Auditing Ops refers the audit out to a contractor, it will not obtain \n"
"                insurance (professional liability, workers' compensation, general liability, auto, etc.) for the auditor or his/her/its \n"
"                employees. Independent auditors agree by a separate referral agreement to obtain his/her own insurance coverage and furnish \n"
"                a copy of the certificate of insurance to Primus Auditing Ops. Furthermore, in those instances in which an independent \n"
"                auditor is retained, Primus Auditing Ops will be acting in the sole capacity of independent contractor and any information \n"
"                or data received will be merely transmitted between parties, making no independent judgment, representations or warranties \n"
"                as to the facts, observations or inferences made relative to same.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>6. AUDIT AND SURVEILLANCE.</b> Customer agrees and acknowledges free access is required to be made for any scheduled \n"
"                audit, as well as possible random quality assurance checks (depending on the audit scheme's requirements) of customer's \n"
"                operation including but not limited to: examination of documentation, records, and access to the equipment, location(s), \n"
"                area(s), personnel, and full physical inspection of Customer's subcontractors. Customer agrees to allow observers from \n"
"                Primus Auditing Ops and/or varying governing bodies if customer's audit or certification is randomly selected for surveillance \n"
"                for quality assurance purposes. Customer further agrees to grant free access in order to verify continued compliance with \n"
"                certification. Customer acknowledges complaints related to compliance must be documented, and subsequent investigation of \n"
"                complaints is possible, and in some cases may be mandatory. Documentation of complaints and investigation may be subject to \n"
"                inspection during audit or surveillance or at the request or Primus Auditing Ops at any time. Customer acknowledges that its \n"
"                failure to fully comply with this section, either during the time of audit or any other time during the certification period, \n"
"                is a material breach of this agreement and can result in Customer's certification being revoked without further notification. \n"
"                The Customer understands and agrees to perform Follow-up Audits when corrective actions cannot be verified in a desk review, \n"
"                for example, in the event of critical non-compliances.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <b>7. CUSTOMER OBLIGATIONS.</b> The Customer agrees to comply with the points cited in the SMETA audit, under the Ethical \n"
"                Trading Initiative Base Code (ETI), as well as the applicable local Laws. Any deviation detected during the audit will be \n"
"                reported and indicated during the closing meeting and in the corresponding document (CARP), for which Customer must take \n"
"                corrective actions to cure the deviation, and is responsible for entering them into the SEDEX platform Customer's corrective \n"
"                actions, as well as entering them into the SEDEX platform is the sole responsibility of the Customer, to which Customer \n"
"                acknowledges, understands, and agrees.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                In the event that a new on-site visit is required to verify corrective actions as determined in the closing meeting of the \n"
"                corresponding audit, the Customer agrees in advance to pay all costs related to said visit, namely travel expenses, mileage, \n"
"                auditor and administrative expenses. Primus Auditing Operations, for this purpose, will send an individual quote accordingly.\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                <br/>\n"
"                Customer further agrees:\n"
"                <br/>"
msgstr ""

